@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki To OSB Product Consumption and Purchase Integration
	Testing Koroneiki To OSB Product Consumption and Purchase Integration functionality.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| A Liferay DXP Product |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| A Liferay DXP Product |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Liferay DXP Product |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORONEKORONE |

Scenario: Create and view product consumption with purchase
	Koroneiki product consumptions with a product purchase created via API should be viewable under Project Details.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Notes                 | Additional account notes             |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Approved                             |
	| Tier                  | Regular                              |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "A Liferay DXP Product" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |                |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |                |
	| Perpetual               | true                     |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1          | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2          | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3          | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |                |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |                |
	And I create a product consumption for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "A Liferay DXP Product" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Product Purchase        | true            |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1 | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2 | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3 | propertyValue3 |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the Project Details page on sandbox
	And I search for the project with the keyword "Korone"
	And I go to the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the History tab
	And I generate the account ID value for "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate the product ID value for "A Liferay DXP Product"
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for "A Liferay DXP Product"
	Then the history entry in position number "3" with the field value "quantity" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin        |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Purchase |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay DXP Product  |
	| Update Date                 | Today                  |
	| Update Field Name           | quantity               |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                    |
	| Update Field New Value      | 1                      |
	And the history entry in position number "3" with the field value "accountId" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin        |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Purchase |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay DXP Product  |
	| Update Date                 | Today                  |
	| Update Field Name           | accountId              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                    |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticAccountId}     |
	And the history entry in position number "3" with the field value "productEntryId" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin        |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Purchase |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay DXP Product  |
	| Update Date                 | Today                  |
	| Update Field Name           | productEntryId         |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                    |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticProductId}     |
	And the history entry in position number "3" with the field value "additionalProp1" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin        |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Purchase |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay DXP Product  |
	| Update Date                 | Today                  |
	| Update Field Name           | additionalProp1        |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                    |
	| Update Field New Value      | propertyValue1         |
	And the history entry in position number "3" with the field value "additionalProp2" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin        |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Purchase |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay DXP Product  |
	| Update Date                 | Today                  |
	| Update Field Name           | additionalProp2        |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                    |
	| Update Field New Value      | propertyValue2         |
	And the history entry in position number "3" with the field value "additionalProp3" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin        |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Purchase |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay DXP Product  |
	| Update Date                 | Today                  |
	| Update Field Name           | additionalProp3        |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                    |
	| Update Field New Value      | propertyValue3         |
	And the history entry in position number "3" with the field value "status" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin        |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Purchase |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay DXP Product  |
	| Update Date                 | Today                  |
	| Update Field Name           | status                 |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                    |
	| Update Field New Value      | 0                      |
	And the history entry in position number "4" with the field value "productPurchaseId" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin            |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Consumption  |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay DXP Product      |
	| Update Date                 | Today                      |
	| Update Field Name           | productPurchaseId          |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                        |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticProductPurchaseId} |
	And the history entry in position number "4" with the field value "accountId" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin           |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Consumption |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay DXP Product     |
	| Update Date                 | Today                     |
	| Update Field Name           | accountId                 |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                       |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticAccountId}        |
	And the history entry in position number "4" with the field value "productEntryId" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin           |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Consumption |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay DXP Product     |
	| Update Date                 | Today                     |
	| Update Field Name           | productEntryId            |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                       |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticProductId}        |
	And the history entry in position number "4" with the field value "additionalProp1" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin           |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Consumption |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay DXP Product     |
	| Update Date                 | Today                     |
	| Update Field Name           | additionalProp1           |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                       |
	| Update Field New Value      | propertyValue1            |
	And the history entry in position number "4" with the field value "additionalProp2" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin           |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Consumption |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay DXP Product     |
	| Update Date                 | Today                     |
	| Update Field Name           | additionalProp2           |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                       |
	| Update Field New Value      | propertyValue2            |
	And the history entry in position number "4" with the field value "additionalProp3" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin           |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Consumption |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay DXP Product     |
	| Update Date                 | Today                     |
	| Update Field Name           | additionalProp3           |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                       |
